        "original_id": "07d6169c-0dd9-53af-b9b6-ff488b0a6734",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gabe Saporta, John S. Hall\n- Bands: Cobra Starship, King Missile, Midtown\n- Music Releases: The Sacrifice of Life EP\n- Places: New York City\n\nFacts:\n- John S. Hall was born as John Charles Hall on September 2, 1960, and he is an American poet, author, singer, and lawyer.\n- John S. Hall co-founded the avant-garde band King Missile in 1986 and has led it in various incarnations since then.\n- Midtown released its first EP, The Sacrifice of Life, in 1999.\n- Gabriel Eduardo \"Gabe\" Saporta was born on October 11, 1979, and he is a Uruguayan-American musician and entrepreneur.\n- Cobra Starship was created by former Midtown bassist and lead vocalist Gabe Saporta in 2006 in New York City, New York.\n- Cobra Starship was an American dance-pop band.",
